      "title": "Rheumatology, Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor",
      "description": "Department: Yale University: School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Rheumatology Location: Connecticut Posted: Oct 28, 2026 Yale University is recruiting an academic-clinician at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor - board eligible or board certified in Rheumatology and has successfully completed a Rheumatology fellowship. Yale is seeking a compassionate rheumatologist to diagnose and treat rheumatic conditions. The rheumatologist's duties include completing the medical histories of patients, performing medical tests, and creating customized treatment plans. Experience in musculoskeletal ultrasound is desired but not essential. There are opportunities to be involved in medical students, residents and fellow education. The practice is well supported by Advanced Practice providers, clinical pharmacist and nursing. The salary ranges listed below reflect the anticipated compensation range for all ranks included in this recruitment. $180,000-$265,000 · BC/BE in Rheumatology is required · Applicants much be comfortable treating patients across the entire spectrum of Rheumatology · Excellent clinician and educator Applications will be reviewed as they are received. Candidates should apply directly through Interfolio at the link: https://apply.interfolio.com/196547 Candidates are asked to provide their CV, Cover Letter, and brief description of their academic research goals."
